WF-22 — Form Response Handler

## Summary

- Inputs: phoneNumber, rawMessage (the inbound WhatsApp interactive payload containing nfm_reply.response_json with the Flow form fields). Called by WF-02 when a user submits the WhatsApp Flow form.
- Outputs: First-ever `users` row (status=payment_pending), Slack consultation channel created and `slack_channel_id` saved, payment instructions message sent on WhatsApp.
- State Transitions: [no record] → payment_pending. (If row already existed, no transition.)
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-52 (Ensure Slack Channel Exists), WF-50 (Send WhatsApp)

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — workflow triggered by another workflow (WF-02) with phoneNumber and the rawMessage from WhatsApp.
Step 2: Extract form data — parse rawMessage.interactive.nfm_reply.response_json as JSON and pull out: full_name, date_of_birth, time_of_birth, place_of_birth, consent (true if contains "agree"), flow_token. phoneNumber falls back to rawMessage.from.
Step 3: INSERT INTO users (phone_number, name, date_of_birth, time_of_birth, place_of_birth, status, created_at, updated_at, last_message_at) VALUES (phoneNumber, full_name, date_of_birth, time_of_birth, place_of_birth, 'payment_pending', NOW(), NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (phone_number) DO NOTHING RETURNING id, name, phone_number, status, created_at. Per design rule, this is the first `users` write for this user.
Step 4: Check: was a new user row created (id not empty)?
  - If YES → go to Step 5
  - If NO (conflict — user already existed) → go to Step 9
Step 5: Call WF-52 (Ensure Slack Channel Exists) with the new user record. WF-52 creates a consultation Slack channel and returns channelId.
Step 6: UPDATE users SET slack_channel_id = <channelId from WF-52>, updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = <new user id> RETURNING id, slack_channel_id.
Step 7: Prepare payment instructions message:
  - phoneNumber = user's phone, messageType = "interactive".
  - interactivePayload: type="button", body="Thank you <name>! Your details have been received. Payment Information: Amount ₹500. Please send ₹500 via GPay / PhonePe / any UPI app to +91-9653240263 (Chinmay Mujumdar). Once done, tap the button below:", buttons=[{id:"payment_completed", title:"Payment Completed"}].
Step 8: Call WF-50 with the prepared phoneNumber, messageType, and interactivePayload. End.
Step 9: Build "user already exists" reply — messageType="text", messageBody="We already have your details on file. Please continue with the instructions previously sent to you. If you need help, reply HELP. To stop messages, reply STOP."
Step 10: Call WF-50 with phoneNumber, messageType=text, messageBody. End.
